  "userdoc": {
    "kind": "user",
    "methods": {},
    "notice": "One append-only version log per manuscript, installed as a Safe module         on an AUTHOR Safe. A draft is a genesis that has versions but was never         offered to a publication — this contract never holds that offer, so         \"is a draft\" is simply \"the log knows this genesis\". Model:   - `append` is the only write and it is `onlySafe`: the author's own Safe     drives the module, so the author of every draft is the Safe itself. This     is the deliberate simplification over the publication module's     `makeOffer`, which has to reason about who is entitled to publish.   - There is no publication, no whitelist, no deal/offer set and no gate. A     genesis lives in exactly one log, ordered by first append; later appends     add versions to that log and nothing else changes.   - CIDs are plaintext in V1. No encryption, no tombstones, no deletion: the     log only grows, which is what makes `history` a stable manuscript trail.   - Identity is `bytes32` everywhere, same convention as the publication     module: the string→bytes32 conversion is owned by `shared` and happens     before the call, so no on-chain cid↔genesis map exists. Storage layout is append-only across upgrades (INV-3 in the publication spec): `safe`, `versions`, `genesisAuthor`, `genesisList`. `Entry` is a return type, never storage.",
    "version": 1
  }
